<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/italita> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:definition "Leucocratic volcanic rock belonging to the foidite family, formed almost completely by leucite"@en,
        "Roca volcánica leucocrática perteneciente a la familia de las foiditas, formada casi completamente por leucita"@es ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "italite"@en,
        "italita"@es ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/foidite>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/foidite> ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/jacupirangita> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:definition "Plutonic rock formed almost entirely by augite, with some nepheline, perovskite, apatite and garnet. It is the ultramafic end-member of the foidolite family"@en,
        "Roca plutónica formada casi enteramente por augita, con algo de nefelina, perovskita, apatito y granate. es el término ultramáfico de la familia de las foidolitas"@es ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "jacupirangite"@en,
        "jacupirangita"@es ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/foidolite>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/foidolite> ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/jaspe> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:definition "Siliceous sedimentary rock consisting of a granular variety of chalcedony. It forms generally opaque, very rarely translucent, massive aggregates of yellow, red, green or brown colour due to inclusions of chlorite, haematite and iron oxides"@en,
        "Roca sedimentaria silícea constituida por una variedad de calcedonia granuda. conforma agregados masivos generalmente opacos, muy raramente translúcidos, de color amarillo, rojo, verde o pardo por inclusiones de clorita, hematites y óxidos de hierro"@es ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "jasper"@en,
        "jaspe"@es ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/non-clasticSiliceousSedimentaryRock>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/non_clastic_siliceous_sedimentary_rock> ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/jotunita> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:definition "Rock belonging to the charnockitic rock family, equivalent to a monzodiorite with orthopyroxene"@en,
        "Roca perteneciente a la familia de las rocas charnoquíticas, equivalente a una monzodiorita con ortopiroxeno"@es ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "jotunite"@en,
        "jotunita"@es ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/granulite>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/granulite> ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/jumillita> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:altLabel "lamproíta con olivino-diópsido-richterita"@es ;
    skos:definition "Volcanic rock, variety of phonolitic leucitite, composed essentially of leucite, diopside and, in lesser proportion, olivine, alkali feldspar and phlogopite"@en,
        "Roca volcánica variedad de una leucitita fonolítica, compuesta esencialmente por leucita, diópsido y, en menor proporción, olivino, feldespato alcalino y flogopita"@es ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "jumillite"@en,
        "jumillita"@es ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/exoticAlkalineRock>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/exotic_alkaline_rock> ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/kainita> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:definition "Rock formed by the mineral of the same name, with the formula KMgSO4Cl·3H2O, belonging to the class of sulfates, crystallizing in the monoclinic system and occurring as compact granular masses. The pure mineral is colourless, but it frequently presents impurities imparting yellow, brown, grey-green, red, violet or blue colour, with vitreous lustre and varying from transparent to translucent"@en,
        "Roca formada por el mineral del mismo nombre, de fórmula kmgso4cl.3h2o, perteneciente a la clase de los sulfatos, que cristaliza en el sistema monoclínico y se presenta en masas compactas granulares. el mineral puro es incoloro, pero con frecuencia presenta impurezas que le confieren color amarillo, marrón, verde-gris, rojo, violeta o azul, tiene brillo vítreo y varía de transparente a translúcido"@es ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "kainite"@en,
        "kainita"@es ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/evaporite>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/evaporite> ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/kalsilitita> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:definition "Igneous rock with more than 10 modal % of kalsilite, in addition to other minerals such as clinopyroxene, olivine, melilite, leucite or phlogopite. Since kalsilite is not stable under slow cooling conditions, this rock usually forms fine- to very fine-grained lavas"@en,
        "Roca ígnea con más de un 10% modal de kalsilita, además de otros minerales como clinopiroxeno, olivino, melilita, leucita o flogopita. ya que la kalsilita no es estable en condiciones de enfriamiento lento, esta roca suele constituir lavas de grano fino o muy fino"@es ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/kalsiliticAndMeliliticRock>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/kalsilitic_and_melilitic_rock> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "kalsilite"@en,
        "kalsilitita"@es ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/kernita> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:definition "Rock formed by the mineral of the same name, with the formula Na2B4O7·4H2O, belonging to the class of borates, crystallizing in the monoclinic system in the form of sparitic masses. It is colourless or white, with vitreous lustre and varying from transparent to translucent"@en,
        "Roca formada por el mineral del mismo nombre, de fórmula na2b4o7.4h2o, perteneciente a la clase de los boratos, que cristaliza en el sistema monoclínico en forma de masas espáticas. es incoloro o blanco, tiene brillo vítreo y varía de transparente a translúcido"@es ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "kernite"@en,
        "kernita"@es ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/evaporite>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/evaporite> ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/kersantita> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:definition "Calc-alkaline lamprophyre with biotite and plagioclase as dominant minerals"@en,
        "Lamprófido calcoalcalino con biotita y plagioclasa como minerales dominantes"@es ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "kersantite"@en,
        "kersantita"@es ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/exoticAlkalineRock>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/exotic_alkaline_rock> ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/kieserita> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:definition "Rock formed by the mineral of the same name, with the formula MgSO4·H2O, belonging to the class of sulfates, crystallizing in the monoclinic system and occurring in granular aggregates. It is colourless, white, grey or yellowish and has a matt or vitreous lustre"@en,
        "Roca formada por el mineral del mismo nombre, de fórmula mgso4.h2o, perteneciente a la clase de los sulfatos, que cristaliza en el sistema monoclínico y se presenta en agregados granudos. es incoloro, blanco, gris o amarillento y presenta aspecto mate o brillo vítreo"@es ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "kieserite"@en,
        "kieserita"@es ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/evaporite>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/evaporite> ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/kimberlita> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:definition "Potassic, volatile-rich ultrabasic rock with inequigranular texture and macrocrysts of olivine, Mg-rich ilmenite, garnet, diopside, phlogopite, enstatite and Ti-rich chromite, enclosed in a fine-grained groundmass of olivine, monticellite, phlogopite, perovskite, spinel and apatite. It generally contains mantle xenoliths in which diamonds may be found. It ascends rapidly through the upper mantle and crust and is emplaced explosively forming diatremes"@en,
        "Roca ultrabásica potásica rica en volátiles, con textura inequigranular y macrocristales de olivino, ilmenita rica en mg, granate, diópsido, flogopita, enstatita y cromita rica en ti, incluidos en una matriz de grano fino formada por olivino, monticellita, flogopita, perovskita, espinela y apatito. generalmente, contiene xenolitos del manto en los que se pueden encontrar diamantes. ascienden rápido a través del manto superior y la corteza y se emplazan explosivamente formando diatremas"@es ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "kimberlite"@en,
        "kimberlita"@es ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/exoticAlkalineRock>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/exotic_alkaline_rock> ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/kinzigita> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:definition "Granulite whose characteristic paragenesis includes essentially pyroxene and garnet"@en,
        "Granulita cuya paragénesis característica incluye piroxeno y granate, esencialmente"@es ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "kinzigite"@en,
        "Kinzigita"@es ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/granulite>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/granulite> ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/komatiita> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:definition "Igneous rock considered to be the only volcanic equivalent of ultramafic rocks. It is formed from very high-temperature magmas with a SiO2 content of 30-52%, more than 18% MgO, less than 2% Na2O+K2O and less than 1% TiO2. It exhibits spinifex textures formed by elongated dendritic crystals of olivine, resulting from very rapid cooling"@en,
        "Roca ígnea considerada como el único equivalente volcánico de las rocas ultramáficas. está formada a partir de magmas de muy alta temperatura, con un contenido en sio2 del 30-52%, mayor del 18% en mgo, menor del 2% en na2o+k2o y menor del 1% en tio2. presenta texturas spinifex formadas por cristales alargados y dendríticos de olivino, resultado de un enfriamiento muy rápido"@es ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "komatiite"@en,
        "komatiíta"@es ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/exoticCompositionIgneousRock>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/exotic_composition_igneous_rock> ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/lamprofido> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:definition "Varied group of subvolcanic rocks of basic or ultrabasic, more rarely intermediate composition, characterized by a markedly porphyritic texture. The phenocrysts are exclusively of mafic minerals, generally amphibole, biotite or phlogopite and, occasionally, pyroxene, in a meso- to melanocratic groundmass containing the feldspars. They commonly occur as dykes and minor intrusive bodies associated with intrusive rocks"@en,
        "Grupo variado de rocas subvolcánicas de composición básica o ultrabásica, más raramente intermedia, que se caracterizan por una textura marcadamente porfídica. los fenocristales son exclusivamente de minerales máficos, generalmente anfíbol, biotita o flogopita y, ocasionalmente, piroxeno, en una matriz meso a melanocrática en la que están incluidos los feldespatos. suelen aparecer en diques y cuerpos intrusivos menores, asociados a rocas intrusivas"@es ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "lamprophyre"@en,
        "lamprófido"@es ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/exoticAlkalineRock>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/exotic_alkaline_rock> ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/lapilli> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:definition "Pyroclast with a diameter between 2 and 64 mm"@en,
        "Piroclasto de diámetro comprendido entre 2 y 64 mm"@es ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "lapilli"@en,
        "lapilli"@es ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/ashAndLapilli>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/ash_and_lapilli> ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/larvikita> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:definition "Alkaline syenite characterized by the presence of abundant rhomboidal-shaped feldspar phenocrysts which, when polished, cause bright blue or greenish reflections; augite is the principal mafic mineral and it may contain, as an accessory, abundant apatite"@en,
        "Sienita alcalina caracterizada por la presencia de abundantes  fenocristales de feldespato con formas romboidales que, cuando están pulidos, causan reflexiones brillantes azules o verdosas, la augita es el principal mineral máfico, pudiendo contener, como accesorio, abundante apatito"@es ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "larvikite"@en,
        "larvikita"@es ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/syenite>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/syenite> ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/laterita> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:altLabel "residual material"@en ;
    skos:definition "Red soil formed by weathering in a tropical climate, mainly as a residue of leaching, resulting in a concentration of iron oxides and alumina"@en,
        "Tierra roja originada por meteorización en clima tropical, principalmente como residuo de lixiviación, que tiene como resultado la concentración de óxidos de hierro y alúmina"@es ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "laterite"@en,
        "laterita"@es ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/residualMaterial>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/residual_material> ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/latita> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:definition "Intermediate, alkaline volcanic rock belonging to the latitic rock group, with alkali feldspar and plagioclase phenocrysts in similar proportions in a microcrystalline or glassy groundmass; may contain quartz in proportions below 5% of felsic minerals. It is the potassic variety of trachyandesite. Its plutonic equivalent is monzonite"@en,
        "Roca volcánica intermedia, alcalina, perteneciente al grupo de las rocas latíticas, con fenocristales de feldespato alcalino y plagioclasa en proporciones similares, en una matriz microcristalina o vítrea, puede contener cuarzo, en proporción inferior al 5% de los minerales félsicos. es la variedad potásica de la traquiandesita. su equivalente plutónico es la monzonita"@es ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/latite>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/latite> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "latite"@en,
        "latita"@es ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/latita-con-foides> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:definition "Intermediate, alkaline volcanic rock belonging to the latitic rock group, containing feldspathoids. Its plutonic equivalent is foid-bearing monzonite"@en,
        "Roca volcánica intermedia, alcalina, perteneciente al grupo de las rocas latíticas, que contiene feldespatoides. su equivalente plutónico es la monzonita con foides"@es ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/foidBearingLatite>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/foid_bearing_latite> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "foid-bearing latite"@en,
        "latita con foides"@es ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/lava> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:definition "Viscous molten material expelled to the exterior by a volcano at high temperature during an eruption. Upon cooling it gives rise to the formation of effusive rocks or volcanic scoria"@en,
        "Material fundido viscoso que es expulsado al exterior por un volcán, a elevada temperatura, en el curso de una erupción. al enfriarse da lugar a la formación de rocas efusivas o a escorias volcánicas"@es ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "lava"@en,
        "lava"@es ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/igneousMaterial>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/igneous_material> ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/lava-almohadillada> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:definition "Type of lava whose surface is shaped by a series of spheroidal bulges, adjoined or interfering, with a pillow-like appearance. It is generated on submarine floors by the rapid cooling of volcanic effusions, preferentially submarine, and is characteristic of volcanism associated with mid-oceanic ridges"@en,
        "Tipo de lava cuya superficie está conformada por una serie de abultamientos esferoidales, adosados o interferentes, con aspecto de almohadones. se genera en fondos subacuáticos por enfriamiento rápido de efusiones volcánicas, preferentemente submarinas, y es característica del volcanismo asociado a las dorsales centrooceánicas"@es ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "pillow lava"@en,
        "lava almohadillada"@es ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/igneousMaterial>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/igneous_material> ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/lerzolita-lherzolita> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:definition "Ultramafic rock of the peridotite group composed of olivine and lesser amounts of orthopyroxene and clinopyroxene"@en,
        "Roca ultramáfica del grupo de las peridotitas compuesta por olivino y cantidades menores de ortopiroxeno y clinopiroxeno"@es ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "lherzolite"@en,
        "lerzolita lherzolita"@es ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/peridotite>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/peridotite> ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/leucitita> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:altLabel "roca leucítica"@es ;
    skos:definition "Ultrabasic, ultraalkaline, dark-coloured volcanic rock belonging to the foidite family, having leucite, pyroxene and, in some types, olivine as essential minerals. The presence of nepheline is also frequent"@en,
        "Roca volcánica ultrabásica, ultraalcalina, de color oscuro, perteneciente a la familia de las rocas foídicas, que tiene como minerales esenciales leucita, piroxeno y, en algunos tipos, olivino. es frecuente, además, la presencia de nefelina"@es ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "leucitite"@en,
        "leucitita"@es ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/exoticCompositionIgneousRock>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/exotic_composition_igneous_rock> ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/leucitita-fonolitica> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:definition "Volcanic rock belonging to the foidite family, in which alkali feldspar predominates over plagioclase and which has leucite and pyroxene as essential minerals"@en,
        "Roca volcánica perteneciente a la familia de las rocas foídicas, en la que el feldespato alcalino predomina sobre la plagioclasa y que tiene como minerales esenciales leucita y piroxeno"@es ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "phonolitic leucitite"@en,
        "leucitita fonolítica"@es ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/phonolitoid>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/phonolitoid> ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/leucitita-tefritica> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:definition "Volcanic rock belonging to the foidite family, in which plagioclase predominates over alkali feldspar and which has leucite and pyroxene as essential minerals"@en,
        "Roca volcánica perteneciente a la familia de las rocas foídicas, en la que la plagioclasa predomina sobre el feldespato alcalino y que tiene como minerales esenciales leucita y piroxeno"@es ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "tephritic leucitite"@en,
        "leucitita tefrítica"@es ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/foidite>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/foidite> ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/leucotonalita> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:altLabel "plagiogranito, tronjemita trondhjemita"@es ;
    skos:definition "Plutonic rock consisting of oligoclase-andesine plagioclase and quartz, with biotite and amphibole in amounts below 10%"@en,
        "Roca plutónica constituida por plagioclasa de tipo oligoclasa-andesina y cuarzo, con biotita y anfíbol en cantidades inferiores al 10%"@es ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "leucotonalite"@en,
        "leucotonalita"@es ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/tonalite>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/tonalite> ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/lidita> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:definition "Variety of chert, grey or black in colour due to its carbonaceous matter content, with radiolarians, formed by chalcedony and cryptocrystalline quartz"@en,
        "Variedad del sílex, de color gris o negro debido su contenido de materia carbonosa, con radiolarios, formada por calcedonia y cuarzo criptocristalino"@es ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "lydite"@en,
        "lidita"@es ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/non-clasticSiliceousSedimentaryRock>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/non_clastic_siliceous_sedimentary_rock> ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/lignito> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:definition "Consolidated-appearing coal variety, brown to blackish in colour, without lustre, with recognizable plant fragments and fine-grained organic matrix. Its carbon content is 60-75% and the volatile matter content is 46-63%"@en,
        "Variedad de carbón de aspecto consolidado, color pardo a negruzco, sin brillo, con fragmentos de plantas reconocibles y matriz orgánica de grano fino. su contenido en carbono es del 60-75% y el de volátiles, del 46-63%"@es ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/lignite>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/lignite> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "lignite"@en,
        "lignito"@es ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/lignito-negro> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:definition "Variety of lignite, black in colour, silky lustre and harder than brown lignite"@en,
        "Variedad del lignito, de color negro, brillo sedoso y más dura que el lignito pardo"@es ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "black lignite"@en,
        "lignito negro"@es ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/lignite>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/lignite> ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/lignito-pardo> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:definition "Variety of lignite, brown in colour, matt lustre, laminated appearance and fibrous structure"@en,
        "Variedad del lignito, de color pardo, brillo mate, aspecto laminado y estructura fibrosa"@es ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "brown lignite"@en,
        "lignito pardo"@es ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/lignite>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/lignite> ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/lignito-sapropelico> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:definition "Sapropelic series coal similar to humic lignite but of homogeneous appearance and non-stratified appearance. Its carbon content is 60-70% and the volatile matter content is 52-63%"@en,
        "Carbón de la serie sapropélica semejante al lignito húmico, pero de aspecto homogéneo y apariencia no estratificada. su contenido en carbono es del 60-70% y el de volátiles, del 52-63%"@es ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "sapropelic lignite"@en,
        "lignito sapropélico"@es ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/lignite>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/lignite> ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/limburgita> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:definition "Basaltic rock in which no fundamental leucocratic mineral appears, replaced by glass. Chemically, it is equivalent to basalt, basanite or olivine nephelinite"@en,
        "Roca basáltica en la que no aparece ningún mineral fundamental leucocrático, en cuyo lugar hay vidrio. químicamente, equivale a basalto, basanita o nefelinita olivínica"@es ;
    skos:inScheme <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:prefLabel "limburgite"@en,
        "limburgita"@es ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/basalt>,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/basalt> ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    adms:status "Válido" .

<https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/limo> a skos:Concept ;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme> ;
    skos:definition "Pelitic sediment in which the ratio of silt-size to clay-size components exceeds 2:1"@en,
        "Sedimento pelítico en el que la relación de componentes de tamaño limo a arcilla es superior a 2:1"@es ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/silt>,
